{"data":"{\"stream\":true,\"stream_options\":{\"include_usage\":true},\"tools\":[{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Read text with one-based inclusive start_line/end_line. Optional max_bytes bounds the read; job reports cap inline output and preserve the full result on disk.\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"start_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"end_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"max_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"List immediate entries, sorted by name; directories end with /.\",\"name\":\"list_directory\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Search files recursively using a regular expression. context_lines defaults to zero. Output uses grep path:line:text and path-line-context with merged windows.\",\"name\":\"search_files\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"context_lines\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"pattern\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Write text, creating parent directories. Existing files require overwrite:true unless append:true. Append preserves existing content.\",\"name\":\"write_file\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"overwrite\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"append\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"content\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Replace one exact, unique old_text anchor with new_text. Zero or multiple matches refuse without changing the file; read and provide a more specific anchor.\",\"name\":\"edit_file\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"old_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"new_text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"old_text\",\"new_text\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Start a fresh /bin/sh in a PTY. cwd applies only to this call, relative to the workspace. Merged output and exit_code stay on disk; a running report is a handle, not cancellation. ai_callback_delay is seconds (default 3); pattern matches unseen output; max_output_bytes defaults to 16384.\",\"name\":\"run_command\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"cwd\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"command\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Wait for a job, including a finished job. Return only unseen output; waiting does not stop execution.\",\"name\":\"wait_for_job\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Send a line of input to a running PTY job, then wait. A missing trailing newline is added.\",\"name\":\"send_input\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"input\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\",\"input\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Kill a job's process group. Go-only work is marked killed but its goroutine cannot be stopped.\",\"name\":\"kill_job\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"handle\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"required\":[\"handle\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Set one-shot wait/output limits for the very next call, whichever tool it is. That call reports consumption; explicit call arguments override these limits.\",\"name\":\"tool_limits\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"ai_callback_delay\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Seconds before looking again, default 3; never a job deadline\"},\"ai_callback_pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Regex on unseen output\"},\"max_output_bytes\":{\"type\":\"integer\",\"description\":\"Inline output byte cap, default 16384\"}},\"required\":[]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Checkpoint at a completed micro-goal. Write text with what succeeded, what failed, source locations and next steps. Removes all tool traffic but preserves conversation and this note.\",\"name\":\"micro_handoff\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"]}},\"type\":\"function\"},{\"function\":{\"description\":\"Keep the previous batch of tool results instead of automatic stubbing on supported models. Does not keep results of tools called alongside this call.\",\"name\":\"keep_tool_results\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{}}},\"type\":\"function\"}],\"model\":\"gpt-4o-mini\",\"max_completion_tokens\":1024,\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You are a helpful assistant built from raw HTTP calls in Chapter 1 of The Art of Building AI Coding Agents. Answer briefly.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"In the Cedar Lantern project (release code CL-721), I decided against automatic deletion of imported notes because the support team needs original notes to address customer-reported mistakes. The design maintains an archive for source notes and separately stores accepted summaries, requiring each summary to retain a source identifier. Morgan oversees the archive review, scheduled for October 18. We have yet to resolve whether attachments should be archived with the summaries or kept separately. The default retention is thirty days, and a failed summarization must keep the original note accessible. Previously, the cleanup process was tied to the arrival of requests, risking deletion of unreviewed work in response to unrelated requests. We shifted cleanup to a defined completed-review boundary, which is crucial to ensure notes are cleared only post thorough review, thus protecting unreviewed work from inadvertent deletion.\"}]}","event":"request"}
